So, I had this obviously-too-paranoid fear that there were
dozens of players in the tournament camping big-ticket bad
boys, and that the last hour or so would be a big spree of
hundred-million-point ascensions. Add that to the odd fact
that i had completely lost track of even approximately how
many points i had. this is because, not being able to find
a unique and creative way to run up the score on my own, I
instead went for the sampler plate.      aided by an early
/oW and a bones pile from bourland, everything came pretty
easily. i actually had gone through medusa ( where i found
pretty much all of clan EIT in statue form ) and the whole
castle before i even remembered the quest.      everything
was pretty much uneventful: i had the full Grayswandir And
Saber Silver Ascension Kit (tm) and had begun to stockpile
other class' quest artifact before i had even reached Hell
or done anything really fun.       the first course on the
point-mongering sampler plate was Mr. Asmodeus. when i got
to him, i ever-so-slowly led him all the way up to Sobokan
and my cache of chickatrice corpses in the deep freeze. (I
had layed alot of eggs as a cocktice, but i let them hatch
and then let the resulting chickies go feral, so as to get
a more reliable stoning supply. it worked perfectly.) but,
as i was merely an archaeologist, with very limited energy
regaining ability, the process of stone/restore was rather
inefficient, and eventually, one of his demons got hold of
a wand and shattered him. so, back down i go, plucking the
book of the dead, grabbing the amulet, taming an archon on
the way, and settin up camp once more in Sokoban. it turns
out that you can be a lot more careless with Rodney, since
even if he gets shattered and turned to meatballs, he will
still come back. mmm... meatballs... <drool> um, yeah, but
anyway, the inefficiency problem was still there. (i never
got the eye of aethiopica, more the fool me for using wish
slots on other artifacts first.) so, at some point, i gave
up, consolidated my cache, and took a stroll to the astral
plane, slaughtering everything in my path.       i lost my
first archon, but picked up two more, twins affectionately
named Seriph and Sans-Seriph. <grin> but i walked into the
portal on the plane of water too soon, so, sadly, they got
left behind. I was not exactly sure what i was going to do
to poor ol Pestilence at this point, but i blocked off the
other two with jellies anyway (i never even got within ten
squares of Death or Famine. i lacked a wish for a boulder,
but luckily i found a magic lamp as i was clearing out the
neutral temple. i'm lucky.       So, i set up camp, and my
keyboard macros added to the +7 halberd was of course also
inefficent due to being unskilled in polearms, but clearly
it worked well enough. Pesty escaped more than once due to
poor timing with the Ki-rin, Archons, and Titans who began
to build up outside. but eventually every space was filled
and i had tamed everything in the 11x11 area that i could,
and after two titan-made boulders blocked off the entrance
from my sight, it became very difficult to get to the loot
under Pestilence, so i settled into a nice, long tedium of
pressing F1.      i slowly ramped up how many sequences of
apply/push-boulder my macro would do each turn, and in the
end, near 3am eastern time, i was in a panic because i had
gotten carried away and the server wasn't catching up with
my key presses fast enough, but when that finally finished
i was like this, with a few minutes to go (blessed !ofMD):

